rough your edge and the Nov 10 reversal off $53.86. A daily close below $56.25 removes it (price under the 200-day is no longer an uptrend) and points to $54.20. A daily close above $59.82 confirms it. The chart agrees with management's cautious tone: this is the weakest chart of the three producers, just as Occidental has the least upside to high oil.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>Oil under $76 WTI for a stretch: the collars stop costing money, and the question becomes how far above $55 it holds.</li><li>Formal 2027 guidance and progress to the $6B debt target; any early move on the preferred.</li><li>The next report: date not found.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Medium-high. Guidance and the quote were read twice against the transcript in the source research. The absolute full-year ranges, the breakeven and the hedge term were not found. The largest-holder figure is the thin spot: it rests on an undated article. Bars from Webull are adjusted for dividends.</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000797468/000162828026072193/oxyex9919-30x26earningsrel.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Press release (8-K exhibit)</a> · <a href=\"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/10/occidental-petroleum-oxy-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Call transcript</a> · <a href=\"https://www.tradingkey.com/news/transcripts/262300236-\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Second transcript</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000797468/000162828026072198/oxy-20260930.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10-Q</a> · <a href=\"https://247wallst.com/cards/occidental-petroleum-q3-2026-earnings-oxy-01m713nxxbsd3b0yv84rdkb2kj\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">24/7 Wall St</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.oxy.com/news/news-releases/occidental-announces-ceo-succession/\" target=\"